  "Question": "Mr. Patrick teaches math to \\(15\\) students. He was grading tests and found that when he graded everyone’s test except Payton’s, the average grade for the class was \\(80.\\) After he graded Payton’s test, the class average became \\(81.\\) What was Payton’s score on the test?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(81\\)",
    "B": "\\(85\\)",
    "C": "\\(91\\)",
    "D": "\\(94\\)",
    "E": "\\(95\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "An average gives the total when multiplied by the number of scores. Before Payton's test was included, there were \\(15-1=14\\) scores, with total\n\\[\n14\\cdot80=1120.\n\\]\nAfter Payton's test was included, the total was\n\\[\n15\\cdot81=1215.\n\\]\nPayton's score accounts for the entire difference between these totals, so it was \\(1215-1120=95\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
